# Allure Homme Sport EDT — reference-first reconstruction research

Research opened: 2026-09-05; closed: 2026-09-06 (Asia/Bangkok). Status: bounded evidence review complete; no commercial proportions recovered.

## Scope and authority

The target is **Chanel Allure Homme Sport Eau de Toilette**, the original EDT product identity, not Eau Extreme, Cologne, Edition Blanche, an iris flanker, or a Versace hybrid. No historical bottle/batch was specified. The current official product page is therefore the documentary reference; this does not assert that all production years have identical compositions.

This is a research and design record, not Chanel's formula, a pouring card, or evidence of sensory similarity. No candidate has been smelled against an authenticated reference. Exact formula, measured reference headspace, observed similarity, liking, performance, stability, safety and release remain unavailable or NOT TESTED/HOLD. No pipeline was run for this record.

The provisional ingredient amounts considered before this review are **not accepted**. No historical formula is its parent. A subsequent from-zero candidate must be separately versioned and identify every numerical proportion as a reconstruction decision, not a recovered commercial percentage.

## 1. Confirmed public target description

Chanel describes the EDT as fresh and woody, with an aquatic dimension. Its composition description connects Italian mandarin to cedar, then an almond-tonka and white-musk finish. These are brand-described olfactory effects, not measured temporal frames or a bill of materials. [Chanel EDT product page, ref. 123630](https://www.chanel.com/gb/fragrance/p/123630/allure-homme-sport-eau-de-toilette-spray/).

The same page's current ingredient disclosure, code `PS000074A`, includes citrus oils, linalyl acetate/linalool, tetramethyl acetyloctahydronaphthalenes, acetyl cedrene, benzyl salicylate, alpha-isomethyl ionone, coumarin and vanillin. It also supplies natural-material clues including orange-flower, lavender, patchouli, geranium and sandalwood. Exact grade, isomer distribution, quantity, extraction method and source of each constituent are not disclosed. The list is a current website record, not a verified label from the user's bottle. [Chanel EDT ingredient disclosure](https://www.chanel.com/gb/fragrance/p/123630/allure-homme-sport-eau-de-toilette-spray/).

## 2. What the label cannot establish

The ingredient list is not a recoverable perfume formula. European cosmetic labelling rules allow aromatic compositions to appear under parfum/aroma, with specified substances additionally declared; ingredients below one percent need not be listed in concentration order. Consequently, neither position on this list nor absence from it reveals a complete formula or a concentration. [Regulation (EC) 1223/2009, Article 19](https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2009/1223); [European Commission fragrance-allergen labelling explanation](https://single-market-economy.ec.europa.eu/sectors/cosmetics/cosmetic-products-specific-topics/fragrance-allergens-labelling_en).

In particular:

- A disclosed constituent such as linalool can be supplied by a natural oil, a separately added material, or both. Do not turn every label constituent into an additional formula row and double-count the natural's contribution.
- A broad chemical name does not establish a particular manufacturer's trade grade or isomer mixture.
- A note such as white musk, cedar or tonka describes an effect; it does not uniquely identify a raw material.
- Calone, Hedione, Dihydromyrcenol, Helional, Galaxolide, Romandolide, specific aldehydes and Ambrox Super remain **candidate tools, not confirmed commercial ingredients**, under the evidence reviewed so far. Their absence from the disclosed list is not proof of absence from the product.
- The descriptor Eau de Toilette does not supply Chanel's exact aromatic load, alcohol/water ratio, density or manufacturing recipe.

## 3. Reconstruction architecture — explicitly an inference

The following is a proposed design interpretation, not an observation or manufacturer formula:

| Structural task | Candidate design objective | Failure to guard against |
|---|---|---|
| Citrus identity | Preserve a recognizable mandarin/citrus-peel emphasis with enough clarity to lead the composition. | Generic lemon cleaner, a grapefruit substitution, or fruit-candy dominance. |
| Fresh/aquatic connection | Evaluate restrained watery and aldehydic options as a connection into the heart. | Automatically installing a large Calone accord merely because the brief says aquatic. |
| Heart continuity | Test a transparent citrus-floral/aromatic connection into the woods. | An independent iris perfume, obvious muguet soliflore, or disconnected top and base. |
| Woody structure | Evaluate the label-supported woody chemical classes and an appropriate cedar effect. | Replacing the target with dry aggressive amberwoods or a heavy natural-wood showcase. |
| Sensual finish | Compare an almond/coumarinic contour with soft musk support and controlled sweetness. | Dense vanilla-gourmand weight or assuming more musks equals a closer match. |

No timing, relative strength or ratio in this interpretation has been calibrated against the real perfume. Proposed reference-comparison windows are opening, 5 minutes, 30 minutes, 2 hours and 4 hours; they are sampling times, not established burn-off times. Intensity and quality should be assessed separately. OAV ratios must not be relabelled as percentages of perceived contribution or similarity.

## 4. Local-source audit and preservation

`formulas/Allure_Homme_Sport_Luxe_30mL_EdP.md` explicitly identifies itself as a luxury reinterpretation. Its opening replacement table asserts an original Calone-heavy accord, a Galaxolide-dominated musk structure and a historical galbanum removal without supplying authenticated analysis for those assertions. It deliberately alters the proposed original's wood, musk and citrus structure. It is therefore excluded as a formula donor and as evidence of Chanel's composition.

Preserved source SHA-256 at review: `56EEDFAA250C4FD7CF04911F28CC93369D53D758428E14C46D78A1FF804F1FC1`. No edits to that file, other historical formulas, embedded diagnostics, shared engine code or inventory were made by this research action.

A local identity inconsistency also requires review: `data/materials/V.yaml` aliases Vertofix to Vertofix Coeur but lacks its CAS, while ODT text uses inconsistent ether/ketone terminology. A shared name or existing alias is not sufficient evidence of this physical bottle's exact identity.

## 5. Current-inventory boundary

The live canonical inventory was read. A bounded independent audit also checked the newer unified-package stock authority; those checkouts have independently valid but different authority chains. This research does not silently synchronize or change either chain.

- Coumarin 20% in DEP is user-confirmed owned. The newer unified record explicitly retains unspecified fraction basis and a quantitative-dosing hold; the canonical text still lists other Coumarin stocks. Availability is not in question. Do not silently reinterpret the DEP stock as 20% w/w or replace it with saturated DPG stock.
- Ambrox Super is recorded as 25% w/w, with a 3 g active / 12 g total preparation. Mass dosing is supported by that stock record; its stock-solution density is not asserted, so exact conversion to a microlitre dose is not established. The older 30% w/v YAML value is not current authority.
- Galaxolide 50% in DEP, Neroli 10% in DPG and the selected trace stocks require their actual percentage bases where exact active-dose calculations depend on them. Galaxolide's stale 80% YAML label must not be used.
- Neither unavailable liquid Ambrofix nor unresolved Guaiacwood belongs in this AHS candidate merely because it exists in an older formula or a wood module.

These limits concern conversion into an executable stock-specific formula. They do not prevent reference research, ingredient selection hypotheses or a clearly separated ideal mass-composition design.

## 6. Evidence still being checked

Three bounded OpenAI-native read-only lanes checked (1) official product identity/history and variant separation, (2) public perfume-specific analytical evidence, and (3) primary supplier identities and candidate-material roles. The parent independently re-opened the decision-critical Chanel and IFF pages. No credentials, physical compounding, final scientific judgment or release authority was delegated.

### Closed findings

- Chanel's own history dates Allure Homme Sport to 2004 and credits Jacques Polge. [Chanel house history, 2000s](https://www.chanel.com/fr/about-chanel/la-maison-chanel/2000/).
- The original EDT's current official description supports fresh, woody, aquatic, mandarin, cedar, almond-tonka and white-musk directions. It does not identify Calone, a particular musk, a concentration or a time curve.
- The official Cologne and Eau Extreme descriptions differ from the EDT and were used only to prevent variant leakage. No material or proportion was imported from either variant.
- Eight bounded exact-product analytical searches located no authenticated, public, quantitative GC-MS, GC-O or headspace report for the original EDT. This is a scoped search result, not proof that private analysis does not exist. A peer-reviewed flow-synthesis review mentions the perfume as a market example but contains no sampled bottle, chromatogram, batch identity or quantitative composition; it is not formula evidence. [Beilstein Journal of Organic Chemistry review, DOI 10.3762/bjoc.18.76](https://www.beilstein-journals.org/bjoc/articles/18/76).
- Commercial web hits labelled GCMS predominantly concerned other Allure variants or sold imitation formulas. Without authenticated sample identity, method, chromatogram, calibration and units, they were excluded.
- IFF links tetramethyl acetyloctahydronaphthalenes to the broader Iso E Super chemical family, but its product is an isomer-enriched trade grade; the label cannot establish that exact grade. [IFF Iso E Super](https://www.iff.com/scent/ingredients-compendium/iso-e-super/).
- IFF Vertofix Coeur reports CAS 32388-55-9 and identifies an acetyl-cedrene ketone with dry cedar, woody, musky and leather facets. This supports evaluating the local Vertofix bottle for the acetyl-cedrene role, but not assuming its grade or dose. [IFF Vertofix Coeur](https://www.iff.com/scent/ingredients-compendium/vertofix-coeur/).
- The official IFF Vertofix page prints formula C17H26O, molecular weight 246.2 and vapor pressure 0.002926 mm Hg at 23 C. These do not agree with the local 234.38/234.4 molecular-weight record or 0.0112 Pa at 25 C. The discrepancy remains open; no number was silently replaced.
- Manufacturer descriptions support Hedione as a transparent floral-diffusion tool, Dihydromyrcenol as a fresh citrus/aromatic tool and Calone as a watery/marine tool. These remain reconstruction tools, not evidence of presence in Chanel's formula. [dsm-firmenich Hedione](https://studio.dsm-firmenich.com/product/hedioner-pe-964898), [Dihydromyrcenol](https://studio.dsm-firmenich.com/product/dihydromyrcenol-pe-938621), [Calone](https://studio.dsm-firmenich.com/product/caloner-pe-918970).
- IFF's public Galaxolide page describes a 50% benzyl-benzoate product, not the user's 50% DEP stock. It can support a general clean-musk role hypothesis only. [IFF Galaxolide 50 BB](https://www.iff.com/scent/ingredients-compendium/galaxolide-50-bb/).

### Evidence ceiling

The available evidence supports a target architecture and a candidate-material selection rationale. It does not support recovered commercial percentages, strict similarity, target-identical headspace, a 2004-to-current reformulation history, or an observed perfume result. The next version is therefore an independent, from-zero current-inventory reconstruction study.

## 7. Next formulation acceptance sequence

1. Close the source review and record which claims remain unconfirmed.
2. Draft an independent, versioned ideal composition from the researched target; explain each selected material's target-linked role and important alternatives. Do not carry forward the provisional quantities as a default.
3. Project that design onto the exact owned stocks, with explicit basis/carrier accounting and no invented density. Any unresolved conversion remains visibly withheld, not silently normalized.
4. Use the existing pipeline for screening only after the input contract is honestly represented. Preserve natural-mixture decomposition and separate exact ppm from proxy headspace calculations. Present the required complete analysis if a pipeline is run.
5. Before any near-identical claim, compare the candidate against an authenticated EDT sample with recorded batch/context. Use matched application, blinded/randomized comparisons where practical, and time-separated observations. No computer score or research consensus substitutes for that evidence.
